because
BECAUSE (conj.):
(1) इति;
poems are not good b.
old, nor faultly b. new
पुराणमित्येव न साधु सर्वं न
 चापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यम्, Mal. I. N. B. Note the
position of इति;
(2) हि (never at the begin-
-ning of a sentence), b. you see that a rich
man feels pain at the loss of his wealth (you
cannot conclude that)
he will have the same pain
when he assumes mendicancy
न हि धनिनो धनापहा-
रनिमित्तं दुःखं दृष्टमिति तस्यैव प्रव्रजितस्य तदेव दुःखं भवति,
S. i. 4.: v. For. N. B. Observe that न हि is
the best way of expressing because...not.
(3) कुतः
or
कस्मात् (=why) with abl.:
here
the word
आयतन
means something else, b. we hear
that it is the bridge of ambrosia
तत्रार्थान्तरं किम-
प्यायतनं स्यादिति प्राप्तम्, कस्मात्? अमृतस्यैष सेतुरिति
 श्रवणात्, S. iii. 1.
