bottom
BOTTOM (subs.):
I The lowest part:
(1)
तल्लम्,
whose b. cannot be touched
अतलस्पर्शः (र्शा,
 र्शं);
who were sitting at the b. of the tree
तरु-
तलेऽवस्थितान्, H. ii.;
(2) अधोभागः;
(3) पादः
(of a hill: v. Foot).
II Fig.: Ph.
one who
has dived to the b. of Philosophy
दर्शनपारदर्शी;
one who has gone to the b. of all śāstras
सकल-
शास्त्रपारङ्गमः, P. i. 10;
you should examine it to
the b.
त्वयेदमामूलं परीक्षितव्यम्;
you are at the b.
of this mischief
त्वमस्यानर्थस्य भूलं
or
निदानम्।
