certain
CERTAIN:
I Sure, undoubted:
(1) निशिचतः
(ता, तं) (ascertained), knows victory to be c.
निशिचतं जयमवगच्छेत्, K. vi;
(2) ध्रुवः (ध्रु वा,
 ध्रुवम्) (unalterable)
know this for c.
ध्रुवमेतदवेहि,
Ki. ii. 22.:
(3) अवश्यः (श्या, श्यं) (=inevi-
-table),
death is c.
मरणमवश्यम्, Ve. iii.;
(4)
असन्दिग्धः (ग्धा, ग्धं) (=undoubted q. v.);
(5)
स्थिरः (रा, रं) (=fixed).
II Convinced: Ph.
yet I do not feel c. from terror
पुनस्तथाप्यतिभयेना-
निश्चयः, V. ii.;
when he was c. that I could
not be dissuaded
यदा नेयं शक्यते व्यावर्तयितुमिति
 निश्चयमधिगतवान्, K.
III. Particular, but
undefined: कश्चित् (काचित्, किञ्चित्),
a c. young
woman
काचिद्युवतिः D.;
in c. systems
कासुचिच्छा-
खासु, S. iv. 1. v. Some.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

certainly
CERTAINLY:
I Assuredly:
(1) अवश्यम् (with-
-out failure),
what would c. take place
अवश्य-
म्भाविन् (f. नी). H;
(2) ध्रुवम् (=unalterably),
would c. have victory
ध्रुवं जयाः (भवन्ति) (with
gen.), Ka. xv. 12,
(3) नूनम् (=surely), c. he
is not as his dress (i. e. as he looks) नूनं तथा नैष
 यथास्य वेषः, Ki.;
(4) असंशयम्: v. Undoub-
-tedly;
(5) नियतम् (fixedly);
would c. give
permission
नियतमनुज्ञास्यति, D.;
(6) निश्चितम्, N. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=112" target="_blank">Page112</a>]
com.
