<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

difficulty
DIFFICULTY:
I Arduousness:
(1) काठिन्यम्;
(2) वैषम्यम्।
Without any d.:
अनासायेन
or
सुखेनः
v. Easily.
With d.:
कथमपि (=somehow),
fixing his speech (i. e. controlling his emo-
tions)
with great d.:
कथं कथमपि वचनं संस्थाप्य, V.
ii.;
(2) कथञ्चन
or
कथञ्चित् (=कथमपि),
controlled
their minds with d.:
कथञ्चिदीशा मनसां बभूवुः,
Ku. iii. 34.; दुःखेन, was able to feed with d.
दुःखेन भोजयितुं शशाकः।: Si. v. 51.;
(4) कृच्छ्रेण,
Ki. iii. 42.;
(5) कष्टेन, with great d.:
महाकष्टेन, M. n.
II Something difficult:
(1) कृच्छ्रम्,
in d. s:
कृच्छ्रेषु, Ki. xi. 75.;
(2)
सङ्कटम् (=straits),
his understanding not failing
in d. s:
कार्यसङ्कटेष्वविषण्णधीः, K.;
(3) विघ्नः
(=obstacle: q. v.);
(4) expr. by adj.,
d. s of grammar:
व्याकरणस्य विषमाणि;
may
everybody overcome his d. s:
सर्वस्तरतु दुर्गाणि, V.
III Embarrassment, perplexity: q. v.
IV
An objection: q. v.
