disgrace
DISGRACE (subs.):
I Disfavour: q. v.
II
Dishonour, ignominy:
(1) अप(व)मानम्,
whose notions of honour and d. have been erased
by decrepitude:
जरावलुप्तमानावमानचित्तः, D.;
(2)
अव-मानना, वि-, (the act), Ku.;
(3) अभिभवः
or
पराभवः (rarely अभिभूतिः
or
पराभूतिः)
(= humiliation),
from fear of d.:
अभिभूति-
भयात्, Ki.;
(4) निकृतिः
or
न्यक्कारः (= insult),
the d. of being removed from the first seat:
अग्रासनापनयजा निकृतिः, Mu.
III That which
brings disgrace. Ph.:
there is nobody without
some d.:
नास्त्यकलङ्कः कोऽपि, Va.;
the d. to the
Paulastya race:
पौलस्त्यकुलपांसनः, Vi.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

