divide
DIVIDE (v. t.):
I To apportion:
(1) भजति
(commonly) वि-, प्रवि-, सं-, (भज्, c. 1.),
after the demise of the father, the sons should d.
his property:
पितर्यूर्द्धं गते पुत्रा विभजेयुर्धनं पितुः, N.
s.;
d. d among the two wives:
पत्न्योर्विभेजे, R.
x. 54.;
(2) वण्टयति (वण्ट्, c. 10.),
the rest
should be d. d:
शेषं वण्टनीयम्, Viv.
II In
arith:
(1) भजति, वि-, d. ing (we)
get the quo-
tient:
भजनाल्लब्धो गुण्यः, Li.;
(2) हरति (हृ, c. 1.)
d. d by the remainder:
शेषैर्हृतः (ता, तं), Li.
III To sever, separate, cut into pieces:
q. v.: विभजति,
as the Meru was not d. d and
made over to the beggars:
विभज्य मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात्कृतः,
N.
To d. into two:
द्विधाकरोति;
into three
parts:
त्रिधाकरोति, Ve.
IV In opinion or
interest: Ph.: (they are)
neither combined nor
d. d:
न संहता न भिन्नवृत्तयः, Ki. i. 19.
