examination
EXAMINATION: परीक्षा,
e. of gems:
रत्नपरीक्षा,
Mal.;
e. -in-chief:
*पूर्वपरीक्षा;
post mortem
e.:
*प्रेतपरीक्षा;
e. of urine:
मूत्रपरीक्षा, Bha.;
after e. (of a book): परीक्ष्य, Mal.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

examine
EXAMINE (v.): परीक्षते, सं-, (ईक्ष्, c. 1.),
one
should e. and then form association:
सङ्गतं परीक्ष्य
 कर्तव्यम्, Sa.;
shall e. a sick man by look, touch
and question:
दर्शनस्पर्शनप्रश्नै रोगिणं परीक्षेत, Bha.;
shall not e. witnesses in all cases of violence:
साहसेसु च सर्वेषु न परीक्षेत साक्षिणः, N. s.
