falsify
FALSIFY (v.t.):
I To counterfeit^1; forge.
II
To prove^2 to be false:
(1) मिथ्याकरोति,
 वितथीकरोति, etc., if you f. your own saying:
मिथ्याकरोषि चेत् स्वीयं भाषितम्, A. r.;
(2) अनृतं
(f. तां) करोति;
you should not f. it:
तत्त्वया
 नानृतं कार्यम्, V. p.
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.
[2] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.
