firm
FIRM: (adj.):
(1) दृढः (डा, डं),
made a bridge f.
er than the friendship of Sugriva:
सुग्रीवसख्यादपि
 दृढं सेतुमकरोत्।, Ma. n. vi. 30.;
seeing the attack
was very f.:
दृढतरमभियोगं वीक्ष्य, Vi. vi. 27;
to
make it more f.:
दृढतरीकर्तुम्, D. iii.;
(2) स्थिरः
(रा, रं) (= constant: q.v.),
f. -minded:
स्थिरधीः,
R. viii. 88.;
of f. instruction^1:
स्थिरोपदेशः (शा,
 शं), Ku. i. 30.
[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210319. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/53.
