kind
KIND (subs.):
I Race, genus: जातिः।
II Sort:
(1) भेदः,
k. s. of heroes:
नायकभेदाः, Sah.;
(2)
प्रकारः (of things etc.);
(3) -विधः (धा, धं) in
comp.,
of three k. s:.
त्रिविधः (धा, धं);
of the same
k.:
तथाविधः (धा, धं);
of how many k. s:
कतिविधः
(धा, धं). Ph.: (a) a kind of = somewhat:
q.v.; (b) in k.: i. e. not in money: expr.
by the commodity implied.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

kind
KIND (adj.):
I Generous, merciful:
(1)
दयालु (mfn.),
as if by k. penance:
दयालुनेव तपसा,
Ki. vi. 27.;
(2) दयावत् (f. ती) (of persons
only);
(3) सदयः (या, यं). Ph.:
k. act:
उपकारः:
v. Good (subs.).
II Of words:
(1) प्रियः
(या, यं);
(2) मधुरः (रा, रं).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

