lead
LEAD (v. t.):
I To guide:
(1) नयति (नी, c. 1.)
(= to conduct: q. v.);
(2) आदिशति (दिश्,
c. 6 (with gen.)
or
आदेशयति (c. of दिश्)
(in showing),
l. me the way:
आदिशतु मे मार्गम्,
V
ii. Ph.:
with the hand led the daughter of
the Chief Mountain to the marriage chamber:
क्षितिधरपतिकन्यामाददानः करेण॥॥।कौतुकागारमागात्,
Ku. vii. 94.;
led by her finger:
त्वदीयामङ्गुलिमव-
लम्ब्य, R. iii. 25.;
l. to success:
सिद्धिं नयति, Ki.
II To command: q. v.: अधितिष्ठति (स्था,
c. l.). Ph.:
led by whom:
यं पुरस्कृत्य, Ku.
ii. 52.
III To go before: पुरो गच्छति (गम्,
c. l.), etc. (with gen.).
IV To pass, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=411" target="_blank">Page411</a>]
spend: q. v.: नयति: v. To influence: हरति
(हृ, c. 1.).
