let
LET:
I To allow, permit: q. v.
II As
sign of imper. mood:
(1) by लोट्,
let him
be entirely so:
तथाविधस्तावदशेषमस्तु सः, Ku.;
l. him say all he thinks proper to say:
उच्यतां स
 वचनीयमशेषम्, Ki.;
l. it be what may be:
यदस्तु
 तदस्तु, Ma.;
(2) by लुङ् after मा, l. it never
come to pass:
मा स्म भूत्, Ki.;
l. not cupid enchant
you:
मा मूमुहद्भवन्तमनन्यजन्मा, Ma.
III To
lease: भाटकेन ददाति, (दा, c. 3.).
IV Of
blood: स्रावयति (c. of स्रु): v. Bleed.
