lie
LIE (v.):
I To speak falsely: अनृतं वदति
(वद्, c. 1.), etc.
II To be prostrate, stret-
-ched out: शेते (शी, c. 2 (with loc.), अधि-
(with acc.),
he must be lying in this tank:
नूनं
 तेन सरसीमेनामधिशयितेन मवितव्यम्, Ve. vi.
III
To remain, rest: q. v.: आस्ते (आस्, c. 2.).
IV To lodge: वसति (वस्, c. 1.).
V To
consist, be included: q. v.: अन्तर्भवति।
VI
To be situated: expr. with अवस्थितः (ता,
 तं): v. Situated.
VII To be sustainable:
perh. वर्तते (वृत्, c. 1.); gen. expr. with
पश्यति (= to see). Ph.:
“for that has ever lain
at their hearts”:
*तेषामेतद्धि सन्ततं मनसि स्थितम्;
l. in the way:
अन्तरायो मवति; l. hard upon:
पीडयति (पीड्, c. 10).
