mischief
MISCHIEF:
I Harm, injury:
(1) अपकारः;
(2) हिंसा (in old writers):
if cattle commit m.
to crops:
धान्यं विहिंस्युः पशवो यदि, M. Ph.:
m. to (lit. destruction of) crops by cattle, etc.:
शस्यघातो गवादिमिः, N.s.
II Damage, loss:
q. v.: हानिः।
