miserable
MISERABLE:
(1) कृपण (f. णा) (= mean), yet
m. (men) bear distress at the door of the rich:
सहन्ते सन्तापं तदपि धनिनां द्वारि कृपणाः, J.;
(2)
दीनः (ना, नं) (= wretched), very m. condition:
सुदीना दशा, Ku.;
(3) दुःखितः (ता, तं) (= un-
-happy), surely the poor fellow is m. like me:
नूनमहमिव दुःखितस्तपस्वी, Mu. vi.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

