miss
MISS (subs.):
I Loss.: q. v.
II Error:
q. v.
III Opposed to hit: भङ्गः।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

miss
MISS (v.):
I Not to hit:
(1) मोघीभवति (= be
frustrated: q. v.);
(2) with न पतति (पत्, c.
1 (= not to fall).
II Not to attain:
q. v.: न लभते (लभ्, c. 1.).
III To omit, pass
by: expr. with जहाति (हा, c. 2.); etc. (= to
abandon),
to m. an opportunity:
अवसरं जहाति
or
क्षिपति (= throw away).
IV To lose:
q. v.
V To feel the want of: expr. by
circumlo.,
I m. him very much:
*तस्य विप्रयोग-
दुःखं नितरामनुभवामिः v. Also anxious.
VI
To err: q. v.
