particular
PARTICULAR (adj.):
I Not common, singu-
-lar, special:
(1) विशेष- in comp.; p. news:
विशेषवार्त्ता;
p. grant:
विशेषदानम्, He.;
(2) विशिष्ट
(f. ष्टा);
p. mark:
विशिष्टलिङ्गम्।
II Specifiable,
definite: -विशेषः in comp., at p. times:
कालविशेषे;
to p. individuals:
व्यक्तिविशेषेषु, M. n.
on Ku. v. 31.
III Minute: q. v.: सूक्ष्म (f.
क्ष्मा).
IV Hard to suit, punctilious: expr.
by circumlo.,
very p. in dress:
*वेशभूषायां
 महादरः। V. Single, individual: not expr.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particular
PARTICULAR (subs.):
in p.:
विशेषतः;
p. s of a
story:
घटनावली (better expr. with विस्तरशः =
in detail);
“for his p.”:
विशिष्टतया।
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

particularity
PARTICULARITY:
I Lit.: विशिष्टता।
