POSSESSION:
I In law: भोगः, सम्भोगः, परिभोगः,
(rarely) भुक्तिः (= enjoyment),
p. with title of
long standing, without interruption, without
dispute:
सागमो दीर्घकालो निरन्तरो निराक्रोशो भोगः,
Mi. on Y. ii. 28.; p. is a proof of ownership:
भोगस्य स्वत्वे प्रामाण्यम्, Mi.; अधिकारः (?).
To take p. of:
(1) अधिकरोति (?);
(2) गृह्णाति,
 परि- (ग्रह्, c. 9.),
another crocodile has taken
p. of your house:
त्वदीयं गृहमपरेण मकरेण गृहीतम्,
P. iv. 9.
II That which is possessed:
(1) भुक्तिः;
(2) by circumlo.
III By evil
spirits: आवेशः।
