power
POWER:
I Strength:
(1) शक्तिः,
my p. is fail-
ing in a fight with an inferior:
शक्तिर्ममावस्यति
 हीनयुद्धे, Ki. xvi. 17.;
(2) प्रभावः (as disclosed
in effect), excelling the gods and demons in p.:
अतिशयितसुरासुरप्रभाव (f. वा), U. v. 4.;
(3) वीर्यम्
(= strength),
triumphant p.:
विजयि वीर्यम्, Vi.
i. 8.;
(4) बलम्: v. Force;
(5) सामर्थ्यम्
(rare), Vi.
II Ability:
(1) शक्तिः,
p. of pro-
creation:
प्रजननशक्तिः;
(2) सामर्थ्यम्;
(3) क्षमता।
III Influence:
(1) प्रभुत्वम्, -ता,
as they had
no p. they could not extricate him from the mis-
fortune:
न शेकतुस्तमप्रभुत्वादुत्तारयितुमापदः, D. i.;
p. is founded on money:
प्रभुत्वं धनमूलं हि, H.;
(2) प्रभावः,
through my p.:
मत्प्रभावात्, Mah.
To have p. over:
प्रभवति (भू, c. 1.: with loc.),
K. To be in one's p.: expr. by adj.: v.
Able, to defend.
As far as lies in one's
power:
यावच्छक्तितः, K.
IV In Alg.: घातः।
V. Forces: बलम्।
VI A spirit: q. v.
