<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prove
PROVE (v. t.):
I To test: q. v.: परीक्षते (ईक्ष्,
c. 1.).
II To establish: q. v.:
(1) प्रतिपादयति
(c. of पद्),
in the first chapter, we have p. d
that He is the soul of all us:
प्रथमेऽध्याये स एव
 सर्वेषां न आत्मैतत् प्रतिपादितम्, S. ii. 1.;
(2) साधयति
(c. of सिध्), a thing may be p. d without
(regular)
proof:
असतापि प्रमाणेन वस्तु सुध्यति,
S. p. b.;
(3) वि-भावयति (c. l. of भू rare),
and
does not p. what he asserts:
उक्तञ्च न विभावयेत्,
M. viii. 56.: v. Also to shew.
III To
verify: प्रमाणयति (nomi.),
p. ing what Yudhiṣ-
ṭhira said:
प्रमाणयन् वाक्यमजातशत्रोः, Ki. iii. 24.
IV To suffer: q. v.: सहते (सह्, c. 1.).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

prove
PROVE (v. i.):
(1) often by भवति (= to be-
-come);
(2) by circumlo.,
it has p. d to be
false;
तदवैमि कैतवम्, Ku. iv. 9.: v. Also to
turn out.
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

provender
PROVENDER: for cattle: यवसः: v. Fodder.
