sense
SENSE:
I Organ: इन्द्रियम्, s. of touch:
स्पर्शेन्द्रियम्;
s. of taste:
रसनेन्द्रियम्; etc. Ph.:
to deprive one of the s. of sight:
चक्षुषी उद्धरति
(with gen.), D.; and sound is the object of
(the s. of)
hearing:
शब्दोऽपि गोचरः श्रुतेः, Par.
53.
II Perception, feeling: उपलब्धिः। Ph.:
to have s. of:
चेतयते, D. viii. or पश्यति (= to
see: q. v.).
III Soundness of the facul-
-ties:
common s.:
विवेकः;
moral s.:
धर्मबुद्धिः
(?);
to recover s. s:
संज्ञां लभते, Ma. ix.;
loss
of s. s:
धीविभ्रमः, Bha;
one who has lost the s.
of honour by decrepitude:
जरावलुप्तमानावमानचितः,
D. i.
IV Meaning:
(1) अर्थ:,
otherwise the
plural “daughters” has no s.:
अन्यथा दुहितर इति
 बहुवचनमनर्थकम्, Da. 141.;
do not take the say-
ing in its real sense:
परमार्थेन न गृह्यतां वचः, Sa.
ii. 19.; have you comprehended its literal s.:
अपि गृहीतो भवताक्षरार्थः, Sa. v.; as the word
अपि
is not described in the s. of
एव: अपिशब्दस्यैव-
कारार्थेऽवर्णनात्, Da.;
a vocabulary of words
having various s. s:
नानार्थशब्दकोषः, Medini; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=628" target="_blank">Page628</a>]
(2) by sim. loc. in lexicons, रत्न
conveys the s.
of ‘superior’ as well as of ‘gem’:
रत्नं श्रेष्ठे
 भणावपि, Viśva;
(3) मावः। (= purport).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

