without
WITHOUT (prep.):
I Before nouns:
(1) विना
(with ins. or acc., rarely with abl.),
I can-
not remain a moment w. you:
न शक्नोमि मवता
 विना क्षणमष्यवस्थातुम्, K.;
(2) by negatives,
w.
eyes He sees, w. ears He hears:
पश्यत्यचक्षुः स
 शृणोत्यकर्णः, S.: v. Devoid of;
(3) अन्तरेण
(with acc.: rarely),
there is no pleasure w.
God:
अन्तरेण हरिं न सुखम्, S. k.;
(4) ऋते (with acc.
and abl.),
w. a general:
ऋते सेनाप्रणेतारम्, Mah.
v. 150-2.
(5) by part.s, वर्जयित्वा (= leav-
-ing off) etc.; “न भूरिदानं विरहय्य सत्क्रियाम्”,
Ki. i. 12.; “न हीन्द्रियाण्यनुपादाय प्रत्यक्षादिव्यवहारः
 सम्भवति”, S.
II Before part.s: अ (अन्,
before vowels), w. reducing dust to mud:
अनीत्वा पङ्कतां धूलिम्, Si. ii. 34.; w. being seen:
अलक्षितः (ता, तं), etc.
III Outside of:
q. v.: बहिः (with abl.).
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BOR&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a>
<a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bor" target="_blank">Correction</a>

without
